    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13651" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσᾰλεύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lie in the roadstead, ride at anchor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.137
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀγκὐρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					50.22
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				523b33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				685a34
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐν φόβοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					7.3.4
				</span></i>
			; <i>keep aloof from,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.493d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσαλεύσας: ἐπιτηρήσας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">Hsch.,
				<u>EM</u>125.48</span></i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> trans., <i>shake,
				cause to move,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.141
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			 (with fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-σαλεύσομαἰ,</span>
			<i>to be loosened, shaken away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Ren.Ves.</u>
				12.3
			</span></i>; <i>be shaken from one's opinion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				3.26.16
			</span></i>.</div>
